From 7ed8f307cad83ceb2b100e69ddb9a4bced0f0e36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 20:31:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] docs(process): targeted tests at review, the full heavy
 lanes at the cut

The maintainer decided on 2026-11-22 ("Targeted tests, heavy at the cut"):
a review runs the pinning tests, the quick plan, the example catalog suites
by name and the light lane. No PR runs the full heavy lanes and no PR is
owed heavy. The full lanes run at the cut and on the post-merge and cut
runners. A P1 PR under the safety floor runs one targeted heavy step.
`cargo xtask gate heavy` and `--covers` stay as tools, not as a merge
condition. One heavy run took 50 to 140 minutes, and it held the merges.

Fixes #3556

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
